ned, nine in supply, 1 water."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q03", "question": "Can you Reveal with Agents left, and can you later take an Agent turn in the same round? What cards supply Reveal effects and where do all played cards go?"}, "K": {"id": "Q03", "expected_answer": "May Reveal early; no more turns this phase after Reveal. Only cards remaining in hand and just revealed supply Reveal effects, not Agent-turn cards. Clean Up puts all Agent and Reveal cards in discard pile.", "source_references": "Main pp8,12 / extraction 360–379,637–673", "novelty": "Reveal commitment and destinations"}, "R": {"id": "Q03", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [407, 417], "pdf_pages": [8], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}, {"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [715, 746], "pdf_pages": [12], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}]}, "A": {"id": "Q03", "answer": "Yes, you may take a Reveal turn with Agents left; after Revealing, you are skipped for the rest of Player Turns and cannot take a later Agent turn that round. Reveal effects come only from cards left in hand and revealed for that Reveal turn, not cards played on Agent turns. At Clean Up, move every card in front of you from both types of turns to your discard pile.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Player Turns: Agent turns optional; after Reveal your turns are skipped. Reveal Turn: effects of just-revealed cards only; Clean Up moves all cards in front to discard."}, "B": {"id": "Q03", "answer": "Yes. You may take a Reveal turn while Agents remain, but after Revealing you skip the rest of Player Turns and cannot take another Agent turn that round. Reveal effects come only from cards revealed from the remaining hand, not Agent-turn cards. On Clean Up, all cards in front of you from both Agent and Reveal turns go to your discard pile.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Player Turns: Agent turns optional; once Revealed, turns are skipped. Reveal: resolve just-revealed cards; Clean Up moves all cards in front of you to discard."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q04", "question": "May an Agent-turn card effect provide resources to pay the destination entry cost? How many Agents can one card send, and can a card without Agent icons be used?"}, "K": {"id": "Q04", "expected_answer": "Entry costs paid immediately before any card or space effects; cannot use later gains to pay entry. One card sends one Agent using one matching icon. No-icon card cannot be played on an Agent turn.", "source_references": "Main p9 / extraction 425–452", "novelty": "Entry legality and costs"}, "R": {"id": "Q04", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [482, 506], "pdf_pages": [9], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}]}, "A": {"id": "Q04", "answer": "A Plot Intrigue played during your own Agent turn may grant resources before placement, and those resources may pay that visit’s entry cost. Resources from the played Agent card or destination effects occur after placement and cannot pay that entry cost. One card can send only one Agent, using one matching Agent icon. A card with no Agent icons cannot be played for an Agent turn; it can only be revealed.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Player Turns: Plot resources before placement join available supply; later gains cannot pay same entry. Agent Turn: one icon/one Agent; no-icon card only Reveal."}, "B": {"id": "Q04", "answer": "A Plot Intrigue may be played before placing your Agent, and resources it grants before placement can pay the entry cost. Resources from the card used to send that Agent or from the destination resolve after placement and cannot pay that same cost. One card can send only one Agent, using only one matching Agent icon. A card with no Agent icons cannot be used on an Agent turn; it may be revealed instead.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Player Turns: Plot can be played first, and its pre-placement grants can pay entry; later gains cannot. Agent Turn: choose one icon; no-icon cards only on Reveal."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q05", "question": "At a Combat space you recruit three troops this turn and already have four garrisoned. How many can deploy? What if the destination is not a Combat space, and where do recruited troops originate?"}, "K": {"id": "Q05", "expected_answer": "May deploy all three newly recruited plus at most two older garrison troops, five total. Normal deployment unavailable at noncombat space. Recruit from own supply into garrison; empty supply prevents recruiting.", "source_references": "Main p10 / extraction 535–566", "novelty": "Recruit and deployment limits"}, "R": {"id": "Q05", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [597, 620], "pdf_pages": [10], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}]}, "A": {"id": "Q05", "answer": "Deploy all 3 troops recruited this turn plus at most 2 of the 4 troops already in your garrison, for up to 5. At a non-Combat space, normal deployment is not allowed. Recruited troops are taken from your supply and placed in your garrison before deployment.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Recruiting & Deploying: deploy any/all units recruited this turn plus up to two more from garrison, at a Combat space; cube recruits from supply into garrison."}, "B": {"id": "Q05", "answer": "At a Combat space, all three troops recruited during this turn may deploy, plus up to two of the four already in your garrison, for at most five deployed from those sources. At a non-Combat space, normal deployment is not allowed. Recruited troops come from your supply and are placed in your garrison before deployment.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Recruiting & Deploying: deploy any/all units recruited this turn plus up to two from garrison, only at a Combat space; cube recruits a troop from supply into garrison."}}
