{"chunk_id":"fc3d78","wall_time_seconds":0.551213186,"exit_code":0,"original_token_count":3214,"output":"{"Q": {"id": "Q11", "question": "When is a normal battle-icon match checked, which cards qualify, is matching optional, and how is a wild icon used?"}, "K": {"id": "Q11", "expected_answer": "After winning and taking Conflict card face up in supply check another face-up Conflict or Objective with same icon; must flip pair face down for 1 VP. At Endgame wild can match any of three icons in supply, pair flipped for 1 VP.", "source_references": "Main p14,p20 / extraction 770–777,1090–1096", "novelty": "Battle icon match"}, "R": {"id": "Q11", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [845, 853], "pdf_pages": [14], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}, {"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [1225, 1227], "pdf_pages": [20], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}]}, "A": {"id": "Q11", "answer": "After winning and taking a Conflict card face up into your supply, check it against your other face-up Conflict or Objective cards. Matching is mandatory: flip the pair face down and gain 1 VP. During Endgame, a wild battle icon may match any one of the three icon types in your supply; flip the pair for 1 VP.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Battle Icons: winner takes card, check matching face-up Conflict or Objective; must flip pair; Endgame wild match."}, "B": {"id": "Q11", "answer": "After winning a Conflict, take its card face up into your supply, then check it against another face-up Conflict or Objective card there. A matching pair must be flipped face down for 1 VP; it is not optional. At Endgame, a wild battle icon may match any one of the three battle icons in your supply, and the pair is flipped for 1 VP.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Combat winner procedure and Battle Icons: take card, then mandatory match check; eligible face-up cards and Endgame wild match."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q12", "question": "What are the rewards and reversibility at 2 and 4 Faction Influence, and does tying the Alliance holder at 4 steal the Alliance?"}, "K": {"id": "Q12", "expected_answer": "Reach 2 gets 1 VP lost below 2. Reach 4 gets track bonus retained if falling below, can earn again on re-reaching. First to 4 gets Alliance and its VP; tie does not steal, opponent must rise higher. Transfer loses old holder VP and gives new holder VP.", "source_references": "Main p7 / extraction 333–344", "novelty": "Influence thresholds and Alliance"}, "R": {"id": "Q12", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [368, 376], "pdf_pages": [7], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}]}, "A": {"id": "Q12", "answer": "At 2 Influence, gain 1 VP; you lose that VP below 2 and regain it on reaching 2 again. At 4, gain the printed track bonus, which is retained below 4 and earned again on returning to 4. The first to 4 also gains the Alliance token and 1 VP; that VP follows token possession. Tying the holder does not steal it: a challenger must rise above the holder. If the holder loses Influence while previously tied, FAQ transfer rules apply.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Scoring—Faction Influence: 2 VP reversal; 4 track bonus retained; Alliance token temporary VP; tying does not transfer."}, "B": {"id": "Q12", "answer": "At 2 Influence, gain 1 VP, lose it below 2, and regain it on returning to 2. At 4, gain the printed track bonus, which is retained if you fall below 4 and earned again on returning; the first to 4 also takes the Alliance token and its 1 VP, which is lost if the token leaves. Merely tying the Alliance holder at 4 does not take the token; you must rise above them. The FAQ separately says that if the holder loses Influence after a tie, the formerly tied player takes it (or, if several were tied, the former holder chooses). If the holder falls to 3 or lower and no one has 4+, it returns to the board.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Victory Points—Faction Influence: separate 2- and 4-Influence rewards and Alliance transfer rules; FAQ Alliance loss clarification."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q13", "question": "When can Persuasion be spent during Reveal, may it be pooled or split, can you buy a Row replacement immediately, and where does the acquired card go?"}, "K": {"id": "Q13", "expected_answer": "Before between or after Reveal effects; can pool and split. Refill Row to five immediately; may buy replacement with remaining Persuasion. Acquired card face-up discard, cannot use immediately; unspent Persuasion lost.", "source_references": "Main pp12–13 / extraction 645–649,704–730", "novelty": "Acquisition timing and destination"}, "R": {"id": "Q13", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [723, 725], "pdf_pages": [12], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}, {"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [775, 805], "pdf_pages": [13], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}]}, "A": {"id": "Q13", "answer": "During your Reveal turn, Persuasion can be spent before, between, or after Reveal effects. You may pool Persuasion from multiple sources for one purchase and split one source across several purchases. The Imperium Row is replenished to five, so you may buy the replacement immediately if you can afford it. Acquired cards go face up into your discard pile.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Acquiring Cards: Reveal timing, pool/split, replace missing Row cards, acquired card enters discard."}, "B": {"id": "Q13", "answer": "During Reveal, spend Persuasion to acquire Imperium Row cards or either Reserve card, Prepare the Way or The Spice Must Flow. The cost is at the card's top right. You may pool Persuasion sources to buy one card or split a source across purchases, and acquire cards before, between, or after Reveal effects. The Row refills to five immediately, so you may buy the replacement if you can afford it. Acquired cards go face up to your discard pile; unused Persuasion is lost.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Acquiring Cards: Reveal purchases, top-right cost, pooling/splitting, Row replacement, discard destination, and unused Persuasion lost."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q14", "question": "How do Maker bonus spice, the Shield Wall and Maker Hooks affect harvesting and summoning, and where can a sandworm be placed?"}, "K": {"id": "Q14", "expected_answer": "Makers phase adds one bonus spice on each unoccupied Maker space, accumulating; visiting collects all bonus spice. Shield Wall blocks worms at Arrakeen, Spice Refinery, Imperial Basin until removed to box. Maker Hooks prerequisite when specified; summoning directly bank to Conflict, never garrison.", "source_references": "Main pp10,15,20 / extraction 493–522,567–584,835–845,1130–1135", "novelty": "Maker and worm restrictions"}, "R": {"id": "Q14", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [574, 588], "pdf_pages": [10], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}, {"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [621, 633], "pdf_pages": [10], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}, {"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [912, 915], "pdf_pages": [15], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}, {"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [1257, 1259], "pdf_pages": [20], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}, {"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [1286, 1288], "pdf_pages": [20], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}]}, "A": {"id": "Q14", "answer": "At Makers, put 1 spice in each Maker space with no Agent, adding to existing bonus spice; a visitor gains all bonus spice there. Deep Desert costs 3 water and offers 4 base spice or, with Maker Hooks, two sandworms; Hagga Basin costs 1 water and offers 2 base spice or, with Hooks, one worm. Sandworms cannot be summoned to Arrakeen, Spice Refinery, or Imperial Basin while Shield Wall remains; removing it permits worms at any Conflict. Hooks are only required where the effect specifies them, and are retained rather than spent. A worm goes directly to your Conflict, never your garrison.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Makers; Sandworms; Board Space Guide entries for Deep Desert and Hagga Basin."}, "B": {"id": "Q14", "answer": "At Makers, each Agent-free Maker space gains one spice in its bonus spot, adding to any already there; visiting a Maker space collects all accumulated bonus spice. Deep Desert costs 3 water and offers 4 base spice or, with Maker Hooks, two sandworms; Hagga Basin costs 1 water and offers 2 base spice or, with Hooks, one sandworm. Hooks are not spent when summoning. A sandworm cannot be summoned to Arrakeen, Spice Refinery, or Imperial Basin while the Shield Wall remains; after its removal it may be summoned to any Conflict, but never placed in a garrison.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Makers; Deep Desert/Hagga Basin space guide; Sandworms: Hooks requirement/retention and Shield Wall restrictions."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q15", "question": "At what point does 10 VP or an empty Conflict deck end play, what happens before comparing final VP, and what are the rulebook resource tiebreakers?"}, "K": {"id": "Q15", "expected_answer": "Check in Recall at end of round, not immediately at 10 VP. Resolve Endgame Intrigue first then highest VP wins. Ties spice then Solari then water then garrisoned troops.", "source_references": "Main pp15 / extraction 824–855", "novelty": "End trigger and scoring"}, "R": {"id": "Q15", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [902, 909], "pdf_pages": [15], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}, {"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [919, 928], "pdf_pages": [15], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}]}, "A": {"id": "Q15", "answer": "At Recall, after the round, 10+ VP by any player or an empty Conflict Deck triggers Endgame. First, players may play and resolve Endgame Intrigues; then compare VP. Rulebook tiebreakers are spice, then Solari, then water, then troops in garrison.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Recall phase and Scoring: endgame trigger at end of a round; Endgame Intrigue before winner; ordered tiebreakers."}, "B": {"id": "Q15", "answer": "At the end of a round, reaching 10 or more VP or emptying the Conflict Deck triggers Endgame. Players first may play and resolve Endgame Intrigues, then compare VP. The listed resource tiebreakers are spice, then Solari, then water, then garrisoned troops.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Scoring / Victory Conditions: game end, Endgame Intrigues, winner 