ard contracts shuffled face down; two are exposed as face-up offers and the remaining 18 stay face down in the bank. Shuffle four additional Intrigue cards into the Intrigue Deck and four additional Imperium cards into the Imperium Deck. Shaddam is optional. The 10 contrasting-back contracts are for Rise of Ix compatibility and are left out of standard CHOAM.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "CHOAM setup changes and Components: two offers from 20; four added cards in each deck; contrasting-back contracts only for Rise of Ix."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q17", "question": "Under CHOAM, what does the contract icon do, what if all contracts are taken, and how are Harvest, Immediate and Acquire The Spice Must Flow contracts completed?"}, "K": {"id": "Q17", "expected_answer": "Take one of two face-up into supply then refill face up from bank; if all taken gain 2 Solari (also without module). Harvest: visit Maker and gain specified total spice that turn including other sources. Immediate upon taking. Acquire The Spice Must Flow on next acquiring that card.", "source_references": "Main p16 / extraction 880–901", "novelty": "CHOAM taking and types"}, "R": {"id": "Q17", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [954, 975], "pdf_pages": [16], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}]}, "A": {"id": "Q17", "answer": "With CHOAM and available contracts, the icon lets you take one face-up contract and replace it with a face-up token from the bank; without CHOAM, or when all contracts have been taken by players, it gives 2 Solari. Harvest completes when an Agent visits a Maker space and the player gains the stated total spice that turn, including other sources. Immediate completes as soon as taken. Acquire The Spice Must Flow completes when you next acquire that card.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Human contract icon table; Completing contracts definitions."}, "B": {"id": "Q17", "answer": "With CHOAM and available contracts, take one of the two face-up contracts and replace it with a bank contract flipped face up. If players have taken all contracts, the icon gives 2 Solari. A Harvest contract requires visiting a Maker space and gaining its stated spice total that turn, including other sources; Immediate completes as soon as taken; Acquire The Spice Must Flow completes when you next acquire that card.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Taking contracts and Completing contracts; shared contract-icon rule."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q18", "question": "You gain a board-space contract after already sending your Agent to that space this turn. Can you complete it now? Once completed what do you announce, gain and do with the token?"}, "K": {"id": "Q18", "expected_answer": "Cannot complete now; must have held contract when Agent sent, wait future turn. Announce completion, gain printed rewards, flip face down and leave in supply.", "source_references": "Main p16 / extraction 902–907", "novelty": "CHOAM ownership timing and destination"}, "R": {"id": "Q18", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [976, 980], "pdf_pages": [16], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}]}, "A": {"id": "Q18", "answer": "No. If you take a board-space contract after already sending your Agent there this turn, you must wait for a future turn because you must hold it when sending the Agent. On completion, announce it, take its shown rewards, flip it face down, and leave it in your supply.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Completing contracts: must hold at time of Agent placement; completion procedure."}, "B": {"id": "Q18", "answer": "No. You must have held a board-space contract when you sent the Agent there, so one taken after visiting must wait until a future visit. When completed, announce it, gain its rewards, then flip it face down and leave it in your supply.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Completing contracts: must hold it when sending Agent; on completion announce, gain rewards, flip face down, keep in supply."}}
