d pass the marker to the other human, then start next round.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Turn Structure phases; Round Start reveal before drawing; Recall next-round preparation."}, "B": {"id": "Q23", "answer": "The phases are Round Start, Player Turns, Combat, Makers, Recall. At Round Start reveal a Conflict from the top of the deck, resolve a controlled-location defensive troop bonus, then each player draws five cards. At Recall, if Endgame is not triggered, humans return Agents to Leaders; with three or four humans pass First Player clockwise, and in a two-player game return Rival Agents to supply and pass First Player to the other human; then start the next round.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Turn Structure: five phases; Round Start; Recall preparation for next round."}}
