ntroller gets the location's separate visit bonus whenever any player, including the controller, visits: 1 Solari at Arrakeen or Spice Refinery, 1 spice at Imperial Basin. Winning the matching Conflict places your Control marker there, replacing the opponent's. When the Conflict is revealed for a space you already control, you may deploy one troop directly from your supply to the Conflict without an Agent visit.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Critical Locations & Control; Board Space Guide notes visitor and controller bonuses are separate; defensive bonus from supply."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q29", "question": "When two players tie for second in a three-player Conflict, what happens? What if players tie for third in four-player play, or three players tie for first?"}, "K": {"id": "Q29", "expected_answer": "Tied second each get third reward; winner keeps first and card, no other rewards. Tied third receive nothing. Three tied first each get second, no winner/card and no further rewards.", "source_references": "Main p14 / extraction 792–808", "novelty": "Remaining combat tie outcome branches"}, "R": {"id": "Q29", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [868, 883], "pdf_pages": [14], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}]}, "A": {"id": "Q29", "answer": "For a tie for second, each tied player gets the third reward; the Conflict winner keeps their first reward and card, and no further rewards are given. A tie for third receives nothing. Three tied for first each get the second reward, nobody takes the card, and nobody gets other rewards, in either three- or four-player play.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Combat ties and three tied for first table."}, "B": {"id": "Q29", "answer": "In a three-player Conflict, a tie for second gives each tied player the third reward; the first-place winner keeps the first reward and Conflict card, and there are no further rewards. A tie for third gives the tied players nothing. If three players tie for first, each gets the second reward, nobody wins or takes the card, and there are no other rewards in either three- or four-player play.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Combat ties and three-tied-first clarification/table."}}
