d because that card did not send an Agent.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Rival Spies and Schemes; Agent turns Place Spy rule."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q68", "question": "At Hagga Basin or Deep Desert, how does a Rival choose worms versus base spice with Hooks, without Hooks, or with a protected Conflict? What happens to accumulated bonus spice?"}, "K": {"id": "Q68", "expected_answer": "Always take bonus spice. With Hooks and summonable Conflict summons one at Hagga/two Deep instead of base. Without Hooks or if protected, summons none and gains base spice (2/4). At Imperial Basin gains base1. Hagal wall removal requires Hooks.", "source_references": "Supplements p5; p4 icons", "novelty": "Rival mandatory worm choice and fallback"}, "R": {"id": "Q68", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"source": "S", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [265, 269], "pdf_pages": [4], "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315"}, {"source": "S", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [294, 308], "pdf_pages": [5], "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315"}, {"source": "S", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [90, 95], "pdf_pages": [2], "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315"}]}, "A": {"id": "Q68", "answer": "The Rival always collects accumulated bonus spice. At Hagga or Deep Desert, if it has Hooks and the Conflict allows worms, it summons one or two worms respectively instead of base spice. If it summons none—because it lacks Hooks or the Conflict is protected—it takes base spice (Hagga 2, Deep Desert 4).", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Rival Maker spaces."}, "B": {"id": "Q68", "answer": "The Rival always collects all accumulated bonus spice at a visited Maker space. With Maker Hooks and an unprotected Conflict, it summons one worm at Hagga Basin or two at Deep Desert instead of base spice. Without Hooks, or if Shield Wall protection prevents summoning, it takes base spice instead: 2 at Hagga, 4 at Deep Desert. Imperial Basin always gives 1 base spice. It does not lose the bonus spice when choosing worms.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Rival Maker spaces; Shield Wall protection."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q69", "question": "When and how is a Rival’s Combat strength bonus determined, what if Reshuffle appears, and can humans respond afterward? Does a unit-free Rival get this bonus?"}, "K": {"id": "Q69", "expected_answer": "Start Combat in turn order, only with deployed unit: one Hagal card, bottom swords only added. Reshuffle and draw again on Reshuffle. Humans then Combat Intrigue before resolution. No unit no bonus.", "source_references": "Supplements p5 Combat", "novelty": "Automated bonus precedes human response"}, "R": {"id": "Q69", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"source": "S", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [317, 320], "pdf_pages": [5], "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315"}, {"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [734, 736], "pdf_pages": [12], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}]}, "A": {"id": "Q69", "answer": "At the beginning of Combat, if the Rival has at least one unit deployed, reveal one Hagal card in turn order and add only its bottom swords to its strength. If Reshuffle appears, reshuffle and reveal again. Humans then have their normal Combat Intrigue window. With no unit it gets no bonus.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Rival Combat."}, "B": {"id": "Q69", "answer": "At the beginning of Combat, if the Rival has at least one unit deployed, reveal a Hagal card in turn order and add only its bottom swords to the Rival's strength; if Reshuffle appears, reshuffle and reveal again. This happens before humans' normal Combat Intrigue window, so humans may act afterward. A unit-free Rival does not get this bonus.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Rival Combat."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q70", "question": "Can a Rival gain control, defensive troops, battle-icon VP and doubled rewards? How does it handle optional Conflict VP payments and contract rewards with CHOAM?"}, "K": {"id": "Q70", "expected_answer": "Normal control visit bonus and defensive supply troop; win card/match icons; sandworms double. Always buy optional Conflict VP if can pay resources or required Spy recall. Never contracts; each contract reward becomes 2 Solari even with CHOAM.", "source_references": "Supplements p5 Combat", "novelty": "Rival reward choices and module exception"}, "R": {"id": "Q70", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"source": "S", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [321, 332], "pdf_pages": [5], "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315"}, {"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [571, 573], "pdf_pages": [10], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}, {"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [1231, 1235], "pdf_pages": [20], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}]}, "A": {"id": "Q70", "answer": "Yes. The Rival gains control bonuses, defensive troops, battle-icon VP and sandworm reward doubling normally. It always takes an optional Conflict VP if it can pay the resources or recall required Spies. It never takes contracts; a contract reward gives it 2 Solari even with CHOAM.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Rival Combat."}, "B": {"id": "Q70", "answer": "Yes. The Rival can gain control bonuses, the defensive troop from supply, battle-icon VP, and sandworm-doubled rewards normally. It always takes an optional Conflict VP if it can pay the resources or recall required Spies. It never takes contracts; a contract reward gives it 2 Solari even with CHOAM.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Rival Combat."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q71", "question": "When during Reveal do you total, announce and set Combat strength, can you update it during the turn, and how is strength over 20 marked?"}, "K": {"id": "Q71", "expected_answer": "After Reveal Cards and before Clean Up, at any point while resolving effects; announce total, set marker and update as needed. Above20 flip +20 side and count again from beginning of track.", "source_references": "Main pp12–13 / extraction 652–665,733–738", "novelty": "Flexible strength-setting timing and marker overflow"}, "R": {"id": "Q71", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [727, 743], "pdf_pages": [12], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}, {"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [806, 810], "pdf_pages": [13], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}]}, "A": {"id": "Q71", "answer": "During Reveal effects, total Combat strength, announce it and set the marker at any point while resolving, updating as needed. A Combat Intrigue may later change units/strength, requiring marker update when it resolves. At over 20, flip the marker to its +20 side and start again at the beginning of the track.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Reveal Turn—Resolve Reveal Effects; Strength; Combat Intrigue marker update."}, "B": {"id": "Q71", "answer": "During Reveal-effect resolution, total and announce strength and set the Combat marker at any point; update it as needed while resolving, so it is not fixed at the first setting. If strength exceeds 20, flip the marker to its +20 side and start again from the track's beginning.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Reveal turn—Resolve Reveal Effects; Strength."}}
