g ability activates when you play Signet Ring on one of your Agent turns, not merely when you reveal it. Cards of any type can override the usual game rules.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Setup—Leader abilities; Overview: cards of any type can override usual rules."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q73", "question": "How is a Recall Spy icon on a card resolved, where does the Spy go, and is it automatically the same as Infiltrate or Gather Intelligence?"}, "K": {"id": "Q73", "expected_answer": "Return one of own Spies from observation post to supply, usually a cost for card effect. Card recall distinct from the two voluntary recalls for Infiltrate or Gather Intelligence; it does not automatically give either benefit.", "source_references": "Main p11,p20 / extraction 603–605,1150–1151", "novelty": "Card recall destination versus voluntary recall purpose"}, "R": {"id": "Q73", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [657, 673], "pdf_pages": [11], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}, {"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [1277, 1278], "pdf_pages": [20], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}]}, "A": {"id": "Q73", "answer": "A Recall Spy icon returns one of your Spies from an observation post to your supply, usually as a cost for a powerful effect. By itself it is not automatically Infiltrate or Gather Intelligence; those are separate free recall actions with their own effects.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Spies & observation posts: Recall Spy icon; Spy may also be recalled without a card for two named effects."}, "B": {"id": "Q73", "answer": "A Recall Spy icon on a card returns one of your Spies from a post to your supply, usually as a cost for a powerful effect. The icon itself is not automatically Infiltrate or Gather Intelligence; those are separate optional recalls for their stated effects.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Spies & observation posts: Recall Spy icon and separate recall-without-card effects."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q74", "question": "What does the “trash an Intrigue” icon allow you to choose, as opposed to an ordinary discard-a-card instruction?"}, "K": {"id": "Q74", "expected_answer": "Trash an Intrigue of choice from own hand. Ordinary discard chooses a non-Intrigue from hand unless explicitly specified.", "source_references": "Main p20 / extraction 1104–1106,1184", "novelty": "Dedicated Intrigue trash versus ordinary deck discard"}, "R": {"id": "Q74", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [1236, 1238], "pdf_pages": [20], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}, {"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [1302, 1302], "pdf_pages": [20], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}]}, "A": {"id": "Q74", "answer": "The separate trash-an-Intrigue icon trashes one Intrigue of your choice from your hand. An ordinary discard instruction instead selects a card from your hand and cannot select Intrigue unless specified; it discards rather than trashes.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Trashing; Discarding."}, "B": {"id": "Q74", "answer": "The separate trash-an-Intrigue icon trashes one Intrigue of your choice from your hand. An ordinary discard instruction instead discards a card of your choice from your hand and cannot discard an Intrigue unless specified; it does not trash the card.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Trashing; Discarding."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q75", "question": "A Conflict reward grants one Influence of your choice and is doubled by your sandworm. May the two gains go to different Factions? Contrast a single effect that grants two Influence."}, "K": {"id": "Q75", "expected_answer": "Yes. Sandworm doubling of a one-Influence reward gives two separate gains, which may use the same Faction or two different Factions. A single two-Influence effect instead chooses just one Faction and cannot be split.", "source_references": "Main PDF p14 Sandworm Reward Doubling example and p20 Influence icons / extraction 778–791,1123–1126", "novelty": "Explicit doubled-reward Influence split exception versus indivisible two-Influence effect"}, "R": {"id": "Q75", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [854, 862], "pdf_pages": [14], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}, {"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [1254, 1256], "pdf_pages": [20], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}]}, "A": {"id": "Q75", "answer": "Yes. Sandworm doubling allows the reward’s optional cost to be paid again for a second reward; the example allows 2 Influence with the same Faction or two different Factions. By contrast, a single free-choice effect that grants two Influence must put both on one Faction.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Sandworm Reward Doubling example; Influence free-choice icon rule."}, "B": {"id": "Q75", "answer": "Yes. Sandworm doubling lets you take the one-Influence reward twice, choosing the same Faction or two different Factions. This differs from a single effect that grants two Influence with free choice, which must put both Influence in one Faction.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Sandworm Reward Doubling example; Influence free-choice rule."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q76", "question": "A House Hagal card shows a Signet Ring effect for the two-player Rival. Which ability is resolved, and does the Rival need a human Signet Ring card or a Reveal turn to trigger it?"}, "K": {"id": "Q76", "expected_answer": "Resolve the Signet Ring ability printed on the selected Rival card as the Hagal effect. No human deck Signet Ring card or Reveal turn is involved; Rival never Reveals.", "source_references": "Supplements PDF pp3–4 Rival card anatomy and House Hagal Signet Ring icon", "novelty": "Rival Hagal Signet trigger distinct from human Signet Ring Agent-card trigger"}, "R": {"id": "Q76", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"source": "S", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [167, 181], "pdf_pages": [3], "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315"}, {"source": "S", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [237, 246], "pdf_pages": [4], "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315"}, {"source": "S", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [227, 228], "pdf_pages": [4], "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315"}]}, "A": {"id": "Q76", "answer": "Resolve the Signet Ring ability printed on the selected Rival card, not its Scheme. It is triggered by the Hagal Signet Ring effect; no human Signet Ring card or Rival Reveal turn is involved.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Rival Signet Ring and Scheme table."}, "B": {"id": "Q76", "answer": "Resolve the Signet Ring ability printed on the selected Rival card, not its Scheme. The Hagal Signet Ring effect triggers it directly; no human Signet Ring card or Rival Reveal turn is involved.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Rival Signet Ring and Scheme are separate abilities."}}
