{"Q": {"id": "Q83", "question": "What are the three steps of a Reveal turn, in order? Must the Reveal-box effects be resolved in card order, or may the player choose their order?"}, "K": {"id": "Q83", "expected_answer": "Reveal Cards, Resolve Reveal Effects, Clean Up, in that order. Reveal all remaining hand cards first; resolve their Reveal effects in any chosen order; then clean up all played cards.", "source_references": "Main PDF p12; run extraction lines714–748", "novelty": "Q03 asks card eligibility/destination, Q13 purchase interleaving and Q71 strength timing; none requests the Reveal step sequence or effect-order freedom."}, "R": {"id": "Q83", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [715, 725], "pdf_pages": [12], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}, {"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [744, 746], "pdf_pages": [12], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}]}, "A": {"id": "Q83", "answer": "The steps are Reveal Cards (reveal remaining hand), Resolve Reveal Effects (resolve those cards’ Reveal boxes, spend Persuasion, total/announce/set strength), then Clean Up (move all cards in front to discard). Reveal effects may be resolved in any order.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Reveal Turn’s three listed steps; effects in any order."}, "B": {"id": "Q83", "answer": "The steps are Reveal Cards, Resolve Reveal Effects, and Clean Up. Reveal effects may be resolved in any order; they need not follow card order.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Reveal Turn: three listed steps; effects may resolve in any order."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q84", "question": "Before the first round without CHOAM, how are each human starter deck, Intrigue deck, Imperium deck/Row and Reserve stacks prepared? Where do the human Combat marker, three Spies, Councilor and Control markers start?"}, "K": {"id": "Q84", "expected_answer": "Each human shuffles their identical ten-card starting deck and puts it face down in their supply left of their Leader. Omit CHOAM-marked Imperium/Intrigue cards, shuffle the Intrigue and Imperium decks face down, deal five Imperium cards face up, and place Prepare the Way and The Spice Must Flow in separate Reserve stacks next to the Row. Human Combat marker starts at zero on the indicated initial side; three Spies, Councilor and Control markers start in their supply in clear view.", "source_references": "Main PDF pp3–5; run extraction lines102–319, especially C1–C3/E/G3/G6", "novelty": "Initial deck/market preparation and the remaining human component destinations are not requested by Q01/Q02/Q16/Q21/Q60/Q81. These establish playable initial state; not a numerical variant of an existing setup question."}, "R": {"id": "Q84", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [110, 131], "pdf_pages": [3], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}, {"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [214, 227], "pdf_pages": [4], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}, {"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [263, 267], "pdf_pages": [5], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}, {"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [301, 319], "pdf_pages": [5], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}, {"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [334, 334], "pdf_pages": [6], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}]}, "A": {"id": "Q84", "answer": "Shuffle each human’s 10-card starting deck face down and put it in their supply left of Leader. Omit CHOAM-marked cards, then shuffle Intrigue and Imperium decks separately and place both face down; deal 5 face-up Imperium Row cards. Put Prepare the Way and The Spice Must Flow in separate Reserve stacks. Combat marker starts at 0; three Spies and Councilor token remain in the player’s supply; Control markers remain in supply, with no initial location control.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Setup steps 4 and 6; Initial card states table; per-player components."}, "B": {"id": "Q84", "answer": "Shuffle each human's 10-card starting deck and place it face down in their supply to the Leader's left. Without CHOAM, omit CHOAM-marked cards, then separately shuffle the Intrigue and Imperium decks face down; deal five Imperium cards face up into the Row. Place Prepare the Way and The Spice Must Flow in separate Reserve stacks. Each human's Combat marker starts at 0; the three Spies, Councilor and Control markers are among components in the player's supply. The four Influence cubes start on the bottom spaces of their tracks.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Setup steps 4 and 6; initial card states; starting deck."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q85", "question": "Which cards may you ordinarily acquire with Persuasion, where is each acquisition cost shown, and during which kind of your turn may you make those ordinary Persuasion purchases?"}, "K": {"id": "Q85", "expected_answer": "During the player’s Reveal turn, acquire any available card from the five-card Imperium Row or Prepare the Way/The Spice Must Flow from the Reserve, paying the Persuasion cost printed at the top right. Ordinary Persuasion purchasing is a Reveal-turn procedure.", "source_references": "Main PDF p13 Acquiring Cards and p20 Persuasion; run extraction lines775–806,1256–1259", "novelty": "Q13 asks spending within Reveal, pooling, replacement and destination; it does not ask the legal purchase sources, printed price or whether an Agent turn permits ordinary purchases. Q34 only asks acquire-box/reshuffle rules."}, "R": {"id": "Q85", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [775, 805], "pdf_pages": [13], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}, {"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [1271, 1273], "pdf_pages": [20], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}]}, "A": {"id": "Q85", "answer": "During a Reveal turn, ordinarily acquire any of the five Imperium Row cards or Prepare the Way or The Spice Must Flow from Reserve. Its cost is shown at the card’s top right. Ordinary Persuasion purchases occur during Reveal, not an Agent turn.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Acquiring Cards."}, "B": {"id": "Q85", "answer": "During a Reveal turn, Persuasion ordinarily buys any of the five Imperium Row cards, Prepare the Way, or The Spice Must Flow from the Reserve. Each card's cost is shown at the top right. These ordinary purchases are made on Reveal turns; Persuasion can be used before, between, or after Reveal effects.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Acquiring Cards; Reveal turn—Persuasion timing."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q86", "question": "When a human receives a Spy placement icon or a Recall Spy icon, may the player decline the action even if a legal Spy/post exists? Does a Shield Wall destruction icon require destruction, and if destroyed can the Wall return in a later round?"}, "K": {"id": "Q86", "expected_answer": "Ordinary Spy placement and ordinary Recall Spy are permissive: may place/recall. An unpaid optional recall cost gives no associated benefit; Intrigue costs/conditions still must be met to play that Intrigue. Shield Wall destruction is optional. Once removed, return it to the box; it is gone for the rest of the game.", "source_references": "Main PDF pp10–11; FAQ pp3–4 optional effects/Shield Wall; run main lines577–585,646–665; FAQ lines217–228,304–306", "novelty": "Q26 asks placement legality, Q73 asks recall resolution/destination and Q49 asks Sietch option outcomes, but none expressly requests these human icon optionality branches or Wall permanence. Q77 is Rival-specific and uses different mandatory automation."}, "R": {"id": "Q86", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [584, 588], "pdf_pages": [10], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}, {"source": "M", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [647, 659], "pdf_pages": [11], "sha256": "b3ce948cce744b9b6ec8c4de16dbe76d8b393da9a5c7aa77d0d74d3f12aa229b"}, {"source": "F", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-official-faq-2025-01-13.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [175, 180], "pdf_pages": [2], "sha256": "783b74f6aea9b4f0512e68a0581ca0438cb42dd565e2d88e0778b1322ecb5f23"}, {"source": "F", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-official-faq-2025-01-13.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [213, 229], "pdf_pages": [3], "sha256": "783b74f6aea9b4f0512e68a0581ca0438cb42dd565e2d88e0778b1322ecb5f23"}, {"source": "F", "file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-official-faq-2025-01-13.txt", "kind": "text_lines", "lines": [304, 306], "pdf_pages": [4], "sha256": "783b74f6aea9b4f0512e68a0581ca0438cb42dd565e2d88e0778b1322ecb5f23"}]}, "A": {"id": "Q86", "answer": "Yes. Ordinary Spy placement and Recall Spy icons are optional, even if legal. The Shield Wall detonation icon also says you may remove it. Once destroyed, the Wall is gone for the rest of the game and cannot return.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Spies & observation posts says placement/recall optional; Shield Wall rule says may remove and cannot return."}, "B": {"id": "Q86", "answer": "Yes. Ordinary Spy placement and Recall Spy icons are optional even when a legal choice exists; declining a recall that is a cost also declines its associated benefit. Shield Wall removal is optional. Once removed, the Wall is returned to the box and cannot return later.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Spies & observation posts: placement/recall optional; Shield Wall: may remove, gone for rest of game."}}
"}

